"""
Tutorial 7 — Velocity-scheduled linear MPC.

A bank of constrained `LinearMPC` controllers, one per airspeed knot. Each knot is
trimmed on the same `F16PlantModel` this analysis is given, and the plant's symbolic
linearization is evaluated at that trim, so every member is a discrete-time model of
the same airframe at its own operating point.

Measured true airspeed schedules the bank through hat-function weights: one solve
exactly at a knot, two between knots. Each active member receives the measured state,
the reference, and the previously applied command in its own trim coordinates, and its
optimized command is returned to physical units before the weighted sum — the knots
trim to different thrust and elevator, so blending deviations would bias the command.
Convex blending of absolute commands preserves the box and slew limits, which every
member shares.

All ten flight states are fed back directly; there is no estimator. Positions are
excluded, since they advance in straight flight and are not regulated.

`TutorialVelocityMPC` designs the bank, flies a speed ramp from a pitch perturbation,
and writes `trajectory.csv`, `summary.toml` and `response.png`. It extends
`VelocityMPCAnalysis` (dyad/velocity_mpc_analysis.dyad, backed by
src/velocity_mpc_analysis.jl). See 07_velocity_mpc.md for the weights, constraints,
and scope.
"""
analysis TutorialVelocityMPC
  extends F16ModelWorkshop.VelocityMPCAnalysis(export_dir = "results/velocity_mpc")
  model = F16ModelWorkshop.Plant.F16PlantModel()
relations
end
